# Hooks orchestrate, lib executes

## Layers

| Layer | Responsibility | May contain |
|-------|----------------|-------------|
| `app/**/page.tsx`, `screens/`, `components/` | Render UI | Props, markup, Tailwind. **No** Supabase, `fetch`, or MediaRecorder logic. |
| `hooks/` | React state, lifecycle, **when** things run | `useState`, refs, `useCallback`, `useEffect`. Calls `lib/` functions. |
| `lib/` | **How** I/O happens | Pure-ish functions: Supabase, `fetch`, MIME helpers, error mapping. **No React.** |
| `types/` | Contracts | `type` / `interface` for props and hook shapes — not class hierarchies. |

## `lib/` rules

- Export **functions**, not service classes or repositories (no `RecordingRepository`, no DI wrappers).
- Direct calls to Supabase clients, `fetch`, or browser APIs are fine inside `lib/`.
- Split **client** vs **server** I/O when needed (`lib/recordings/client.ts`, `lib/recordings/server.ts`).
- `class` only for thrown `Error` subclasses (`instanceof` in `toUserMessage`) — not for domain models.

## `hooks/` rules

- Own the state machine (`setAppState`, mode flags, timers).
- Delegate I/O: `await transcribeAudio(...)`, `await saveRecording(...)`.
- Map errors via `lib/errors.ts` (`toUserMessage`, `microphoneErrorMessage`) — not string `includes()` in the hook.

## React rules

- **Function components only** — no `class X extends React.Component`.
- Server Components fetch via `lib/` (e.g. `listRecordingsWithSignedUrls`), not client hooks.
- Do **not** add `useRecordings()` for server list pages; keep RSC + `lib/recordings/server.ts`.

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ hooks/useRecordingActions.ts
const { text, language } = await transcribeAudio(blob, filename);
await saveRecording({ blob, mimeType: mime, ... });
setAppState(AppState.DONE);

// ❌ hooks — inline fetch to /api/transcribe or Supabase .from() in the hook

// ✅ lib/transcribe.ts
export const transcribeAudio = async (blob, filename) => { ... };

// ❌ lib — export class RecordingService { async save() { ... } }
```
